adr: 0304
file: selfhost/apfront.pas
kills: generic_infer_partial
why: ADR-0254's tie-break, restored: the question of whether an actual denotes a type is asked at the position of the *first* type parameter rather than the first *omitted* one. Every partial activation then finds a type standing there, is read as a written activation short of an argument, and is refused -- so `VecGet(char, b, i)` and `MapKeyAt(MapKey, m, i)` become unwritable again.
--- old
      for j := 2 to TypeFormalPos(gen, k + 1) do
--- new
      for j := 2 to TypeFormalPos(gen, 1) do
